{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PFromBraidMirror","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PFromBraidMirror","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pFromBraidMirror_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pFromBraidMirror_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L130-L140","doc":"The class is **refutable**, which the previous `holds : Prop` carrier was not: the\nidentity map on `ℤ` fixes every writhe rather than negating it, so it satisfies\n`involutive` and `fixes_q` and fails `writhe_neg` at `b = 1`.\n\nStated as a theorem because \"the carrier asserts something\" is exactly the property that\nwas missing, and it should be visible as discharged rather than claimed in prose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.p_fixed_point_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.p_fixed_point_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L117-L128","doc":"**A `P`-symmetric braid has zero writhe** — derived from the two structural fields,\nnot assumed. If `P b = b` then `w b = w (P b) = - w b`, so `2 * w b = 0` in `ℤ`.\n\nThis is the block's structure paying off: it is a falsifiable consequence that follows\nfrom `P` mirroring the diagram, and it is discharged here rather than restated as a\nfield. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.fixes_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.fixes_q","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L115-L115","doc":"`P` holds `q` fixed. This is what distinguishes `P` from the bar-involution, which\nalso sends `q ↦ q⁻¹`; without it the carrier would not say what the block is for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.writhe_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.writhe_neg","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L112-L112","doc":"`P` negates the signed writhe — the block's restatement of `σᵢ^ε ↦ σᵢ^(−ε)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.involutive","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L110-L110","doc":"`P` is an involution: `P² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PFromBraidMirror","kind":"class","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.lean#L93-L115","doc":"**CONJECTURE (parity closure).** Parity `P` acts as the mirror reflection of the braid\ndiagram — `σᵢ^ε ↦ σᵢ^(−ε)` with `q` held fixed — negating the signed writhe.\n\n`B` is a braid-word type, `P` the parity map, `w` the signed writhe, and `qOf` the\n`q`-datum that `P` must leave alone. All are supplied by the **caller**, so the class is\nfalse for maps that do not behave this way (see `pFromBraidMirror_refutable`).\n\nThe `fixes_q` field is what separates this from the bar-involution: bar sends\n`σᵢ ↦ σᵢ⁻¹` *and* `q ↦ q⁻¹` and is `P·C·T` composed, while `P` alone fixes `q`.\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as\n`[PFromBraidMirror P w qOf]` and are genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:p-from-braid-mirror ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:p-from-braid-mirror","label":"conj:p-from-braid-mirror","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/p-from-braid-mirror.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}